# PR new hunks — what changed since the last review concluded

Last reviewed head: 98cdcd243dc9ccb1ac1dba23b1a221d5519d7b0e
Current head: 68016a7081790803815d49645d5d879d7ae24ebc

These hunks are the re-review scope, together with their interaction
neighborhood (direct callers/callees of changed symbols). Every line
NOT shown here is frozen: a finding on an unchanged line must show that
these hunks make the problem worse (the interaction test) — otherwise
it is advisory digest only, never a review thread.

--- diff ---

# pr_new_hunks.txt Truncated

Original size: 33284 characters.
Kept: first 7800 and last 4200 characters.

The full diff is available in the checked-out PR branch. Use `git diff` or CodeGraph for focused source navigation instead of relying only on this file.

```diff
diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 4e2420707c..bfff9963cb 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -5467,19 +5467,44 @@ jobs:
   # tab. Files/updates one issue per red run, always assigned to
   # ai-teammate.
   # gh-2332 (the v1.0.752/753/754 class): keying on quality-gate alone went
-  # stale when gh-1801 moved the release train AFTER the gate — binaries/
-  # web-spa/build-extension hang off it and release-provenance hangs off
-  # them, so a red train never touched quality-gate's verdict. Three tag
+  # stale when gh-1801 moved the artifact train AFTER the gate. Three tag
   # runs went red with quality-gate green: no draft, no release object, no
   # issue — invisible unless someone scrolled the tag-filtered Actions tab.
-  # The needs below cover the whole release tail and the if ORs each leg's
-  # result; the fa#456 transitive-skip lesson still applies — key on
-  # direct results, never transitive skips. Pinned by
-  # test/ci_red_report_release_legs_guard_test.dart.
+  # Coverage = EVERY post-gate leg that can redden a tag run, keyed on its
+  # DIRECT result (fa#456: never transitive skips):
+  #   artifact train  binaries → release-provenance → release-asset-smoke /
+  #                   installer-smoke / install-pin-bump / train-draft-guard,
+  #   publish path    integration (the #551 hard provider gate) → publish,
+  #   siblings        js-ext-integration, watchdog, step-timings,
+  #                   faui-coverage.
+  # NOT covered, deliberately: web-spa / build-extension carry job-level
+  # continue-on-error (downstream needs see SUCCESS, so they cannot redden
+  # a run); release / binaries-pr / binaries-smoke-gate are schedule-,
+  # dispatch- or PR-scoped (never run on tag pushes); everything upstream
+  # of quality-gate rides its verdict. Pinned — with the coverage set
+  # DERIVED from the live needs graph, so an un-covered future leg fails
+  # the guard — by test/ci_red_report_release_legs_guard_test.dart.
   ci-red-report:
     name: CI red → issue (ai-teammate)
-    needs: [quality-gate, binaries, web-spa, build-extension, release-provenance, release-asset-smoke, installer-smoke, install-pin-bump, train-draft-guard]
-    if: ${{ always() && github.event_name == 'push' && (needs.quality-gate.result == 'failure' || needs.binaries.result == 'failure' || needs.web-spa.result == 'failure' || needs.build-extension.result == 'failure' || needs.release-provenance.result == 'failure' || needs.release-asset-smoke.result == 'failure' || needs.installer-smoke.result == 'failure' || needs.install-pin-bump.result == 'failure' || needs.train-draft-guard.result == 'failure') }}
+    needs: [quality-gate, binaries, integration, js-ext-integration, publish, watchdog, step-timings, faui-coverage, release-provenance, release-asset-smoke, installer-smoke, install-pin-bump, train-draft-guard]
+    if: >-
+      always() &&
+      github.event_name == 'push' &&
+      (
+        needs.quality-gate.result == 'failure' ||
+        needs.binaries.result == 'failure' ||
+        needs.integration.result == 'failure' ||
+        needs.js-ext-integration.result == 'failure' ||
+        needs.publish.result == 'failure' ||
+        needs.watchdog.result == 'failure' ||
+        needs.step-timings.result == 'failure' ||
+        needs.faui-coverage.result == 'failure' ||
+        needs.release-provenance.result == 'failure' ||
+        needs.release-asset-smoke.result == 'failure' ||
+        needs.installer-smoke.result == 'failure' ||
+        needs.install-pin-bump.result == 'failure' ||
+        needs.train-draft-guard.result == 'failure'
+      )
     permissions:
       issues: write
       contents: read
diff --git a/lib/src/cli/agent_cli_waiting.dart b/lib/src/cli/agent_cli_waiting.dart
index 09ab62a34b..8e01f397a2 100644
--- a/lib/src/cli/agent_cli_waiting.dart
+++ b/lib/src/cli/agent_cli_waiting.dart
@@ -43,6 +43,12 @@ final class WaiterSnapshot {
 /// recycled pid's start never matches the recorded one).
 typedef _ProcessTable = ({Set<int> pids, Map<int, String> starts});

+/// The boot reconcile's liveness verdict for one registry entry against
+/// the process table (issue #2267): [dead] drops whatever the age,
+/// [alive] keeps whatever the age — only [unknown] (no evidence) lets
